  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 302.23 Heating oil",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 302.23 “Heating oil” means oil that is:\n\n(a) No. 1, No. 2, No. 4-light, No. 4-heavy, No. 5-light, No. 5-heavy, or No. 6 technical grade of fuel oil;\n\n(b) Any other residual fuel oil, such as Navy Special Fuel Oil and Bunker C; or\n\n(c) Used engine, transmission, gear, or hydraulic oil that is burned for on-premise heating in compliance with Env-Hw 807.10.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Or 300) #10487, eff 2-7-14; ss by #14094, eff 10-4-24 (formerly Env-Or 302.21)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or300.html"
